wiretap-server (0.1.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release; the Python it replaces had no packaging at all.
  * Upgrading from a Python deployment: its unit at
    /etc/systemd/system/wiretap-server.service is stopped and moved aside to
    .pre-deb, because it shares this package's unit name and /etc outranks
    /usr/lib. The new daemon is deliberately not started - carry the settings
    across first. Its disk cache is moved to /var/lib/wiretap-server/ for the
    daemon to adopt, since the unit's ProtectHome= hides the old location.
  * The daemon runs as the system user `wiretap`, not as `pi`.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +1000
